# Vilo core

Static marketing site: **Vite multi-page mode**, no client-side framework or router. Full reference: `CLAUDE.md`.

## Commands

Use **pnpm** (not npm): `pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm preview`, `pnpm deploy`.

No test suite, linter, or type checker — do not add tooling unless requested.

## Pages and routing

- Each route is `src/<route>/index.html` — Vite discovers them automatically; no manual registration.
- Dev server 301-redirects extensionless URLs to directory `index.html` form.

## Assets

- Root-relative paths (`/images/...`) → `public/` (copied verbatim to `dist/`).
- Fonts and build-processed assets → `src/assets/`.

## JavaScript

Islands architecture — see `.cursor/rules/javascript.mdc` for details.

- **Entry:** `src/scripts/index.js` on every page (imports core + island boot).
- **Core** (`core.js`): site chrome loaded on all pages.
- **Islands** (`islands/registry.js`): lazy-loaded per page based on DOM selectors; Vite code-splits each island.

## Styles

Plain CSS, no preprocessor. Entry: `src/styles/index.css`. One file per section/component under `src/styles/components/`, mirroring `_page-components` partials. Section width baseline: `.cursor/rules/section-layout.mdc`, `src/_page-components/SECTIONS.md` (includes collage — see `COLLAGE.md`).

## Git workflow

- Branches: `vilo-<ticket>` or `fix/vilo-<ticket>` off `main`.
- PR into **`staging`** first (staging deploy preview); merge `staging` → **`main`** after approval.
- `staging` and `main` can drift — diff the branch you care about, do not assume they match.

## Scope

Minimal diffs. Match existing patterns. Read surrounding code before adding abstractions.
